| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| shadcn/ui | Source-owned accessible components | Consumer maintains copied components | Tailored product UI needs full control | Components and registry items compose locally | https://ui.shadcn.com/docs |\n| Radix Themes | Cohesive accessible component theme | Stronger visual conventions | Fast consistent UI matters more than source ownership | Theme primitives compose across screens | @radix-ui/themes |\n| MUI | Broad mature component suite | Larger runtime and opinionated styling | Enterprise UI needs extensive ready-made widgets | Shared theme and component packages | @mui/material |\n\n## Ruling\n\n2026-09-05: none \u2014 no design system is adopted because there is no UI; the CLI text contract is recorded in `docs/ux-canon.md`, and no tokens, fonts, palette or spacing are invented.\n\nFor Blade, store pointers only; tokens are owned by zeroh-design.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Positive: no UI dependency and no token source to keep in sync; `designHomes.ux.bindingDesignSystem` stays absent in `roadmap/roadmap.config.json`.\n- Negative: any future graphical surface must reopen this decision before UI code is written.\n\n## Revisit when\n\nA web or mobile surface is planned, or Blade branding is requested (then invoke zeroh-design and store only its pointers).\n'''\nCONTENT['docs/CODE-STYLE.md'] = r'''# Code style\n\n## Lint\n\n`none` \u2014 no linter is configured and the `lint` gate is declared absent in `roadmap/roadmap.config.json`. Enforced style comes from `tsconfig.json` (`strict`, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `erasableSyntaxOnly`, `verbatimModuleSyntax`, `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`, `noUncheckedSideEffectImports`), checked by `npm run typecheck`.\n\n## Format\n\n`none` \u2014 no formatter is configured; match the existing files (ES modules, two-space indentation, single quotes, no semicolons, explicit `.ts` import extensions) until a formatter is adopted through an approved proposal.\n'''\nCONTENT['docs/architecture.md'] = r'''# Architecture\n\nThis file indexes the authoritative architecture homes. Link each topic to its\nowner instead of copying the content.\n\n## Topic index\n\n| Topic | Home |\n| --- | --- |\n| Product requirements and decisions | docs/PRD.md |\n| Stack ruling (tsup + node:test) | docs/adr/0001-tech-stack.md |\n| Design-system ruling (none) | docs/adr/0002-design-system.md |\n| CLI contract | docs/ux-canon.md |\n| Reusable API | src/index.ts |\n| CLI adapter | src/cli.ts |\n| Build and package surface | tsup.config.ts, package.json (`exports`, `bin`, `files`) |\n| Tests | test/greet.test.ts, test/cli.test.ts |\n| Code style | docs/CODE-STYLE.md |\n| Conventions | AGENTS.md |\n| Delivery lifecycle | .github/greenfield-delivery.json, scripts/ci-shard-plan.mjs, .github/workflows/ci.yml, .github/workflows/release.yml |\n| Roadmap | roadmap/ROADMAP.md, roadmap/roadmap.config.json (schema: roadmap/roadmap.config.schema.json) |\n'''\nCONTENT['docs/ux-canon.md'] = r'''# UX canon\n\n## Visual language\n\nNone. The product has no graphical surface; the only user interface is plain CLI text on stdout and stderr, with no colours, tokens, fonts, palette or spacing.\n\n## Component vocabulary\n\n- Greeting line: `Hello, <name>!` followed by a newline on stdout.\n- Usage text: starts with `Usage: greenfield-proof [name]` and lists the options.\n- Error line: one sentence on stderr, followed by the usage text.\n\n## Interaction rules\n\n| Invocation | stdout | stderr | exit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `greenfield-proof` | `Hello, world!` | empty | 0 |\n| `greenfield-proof Ada` | `Hello, Ada!` | empty | 0 |\n| `greenfield-proof --help` or `-h` | usage text | empty | 0 |\n| `greenfield-proof --unknown` | empty | `Unknown option: --unknown` + usage | 1 |\n| `greenfield-proof --help --unknown` (any order) | empty | `Unknown option: --unknown` + usage | 1 |\n| `greenfield-proof ''` or a whitespace-only name | empty | the `TypeError` message + usage | 1 |\n| more than one name | empty | `Too many arguments` + usage | 1 |\n\nUnknown options are checked before help, so an unknown option never exits 0. The API mirrors the CLI: `greet()` and `greet(undefined)` return `Hello, world!`, `greet(name)` returns `Hello, <name>!` verbatim, and blank names throw `TypeError`.\n\n## Binding design system\n\nnone \u2014 ADR 0002 records the non-UI ruling; `designHomes.ux.bindingDesignSystem` is absent and no tokens are defined.\n'''\nCONTENT['README.md'] = r'''# greenfield-proof\n\nA small TypeScript reusable greeting API plus CLI for developers: `greet(name?)` returns `Hello, <name>!` (default `world`; blank names rejected with `TypeError`) and the `greenfield-proof` CLI prints it. Private, UNLICENSED fixture: never published or deployed.\n\n## Structure\n\n| Path | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `package.json` | Package identity (`greenfield-proof`), scripts, and `exports`/`bin`/`files` pointing only at built `dist/` |\n| `src/index.ts` | Reusable greeting API (`greet`) |\n| `src/cli.ts` | Thin executable adapter over the API (`--help`, unknown-option handling) |\n| `test/greet.test.ts` | `node:test` behaviour tests for the API |\n| `test/cli.test.ts` | `node:test` behaviour tests for the CLI process contract |\n| `tsup.config.ts` | tsup build: ESM plus declarations for `src/index.ts` and `src/cli.ts` into `dist/` |\n| `tsconfig.json` | Strict TypeScript settings shared by typecheck, tests and build |\n| `dist/` | Built artifacts, generated by `npm run build` and ignored by git |\n| `docs/` | PRD, ADRs, code style, architecture index, UX canon |\n| `roadmap/` | zeroh-roadmap root: `roadmap.config.json`, its local `roadmap.config.schema.json`, `backlog.ts`, `phases/`, `arcs/`, `lib/` |\n| `reviews/` | Emitted `changelog.json` and `releases/` review reports |\n| `scripts/ci-shard-plan.mjs` | Delivery lifecycle engine: inventory, shard, fan-in, build, attest, release verification |\n| `scripts/check-readme-catalog.mjs` | README catalog comparator |\n|