 once, attest (nightly runs diagnose without attesting) |\n| `node scripts/ci-shard-plan.mjs gather-evidence`, `verify-release`, `prepare-promotion`, `promote` | Release lifecycle in `.github/workflows/release.yml`; promotion runs in the protected environment `greenfield-validation` and stays blocked while `release.provider` is `none` |\n\nLint and e2e gates are declared absent (`none`) in `roadmap/roadmap.config.json`: no linter or end-to-end surface exists. A new test file must be added to the unit command in `package.json`, `roadmap/roadmap.config.json` and `affectedArgv` in `.github/greenfield-delivery.json`; the CI inventory matches `test/*.test.ts` through `git ls-files`.\n\n## Catalog\n\n<!-- repo-catalog:start -->\n| Project | Path | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| greenfield-proof | . | TypeScript greeting API and CLI |\n<!-- repo-catalog:end -->\n\nCheck catalog currency with `node scripts/check-readme-catalog.mjs --project-root .`.\n'''\nCONTENT['AGENTS.md'] = r'''# Repository guidance\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Keep the reusable API in `src/index.ts` and the thin executable adapter in `src/cli.ts`; the CLI never re-implements greeting logic, and it rejects unknown options before honouring `--help`.\n- Publish only built artifacts: `exports`, `bin` and `files` in `package.json` point at `dist/`, which `npm run build` generates and nobody edits by hand.\n- Tests are `node:test` files under `test/*.test.ts` that import `src/*.ts` directly (Node 22 type stripping); the unit command names every test file explicitly, so a new test file is added to `package.json`, `roadmap/roadmap.config.json` and `.github/greenfield-delivery.json` in the same commit as the behaviour it covers.\n- Gates and their exact commands live in `roadmap/roadmap.config.json` and README \u00a7Commands; `lint` and `e2e` are declared absent (`none`) until real tooling exists.\n- Documentation homes: product facts in `docs/PRD.md`, decisions in `docs/adr/`, style in `docs/CODE-STYLE.md`, the architecture index in `docs/architecture.md`, the CLI contract in `docs/ux-canon.md`. Link to a home instead of copying its content.\n- Roadmap work goes through the installed zeroh-roadmap skills against the single root `roadmap/` (`roadmap.config.json` with its local `roadmap.config.schema.json`, `backlog.ts`, `phases/`); never create a second root or configuration, and never point consumer files at plugin-internal paths.\n\n## Don't\n\n- No runtime dependencies, framework runtime, external service, authentication, mobile target, deployment or product remote.\n- No publishing: the package is private and UNLICENSED, and `release.provider` stays `none` in `.github/greenfield-delivery.json`.\n- No invented design tokens or UI vocabulary; the only surface is CLI text (ADR 0002, `docs/ux-canon.md`).\n- Do not hand-edit generated files (`dist/`, `reviews/changelog.json`, `package-lock.json`) or bypass the delivery lifecycle in `.github/workflows/`.\n- Do not lower `baseline` floors in `.github/greenfield-delivery.json` to hide a regression; a baseline change needs `baselineApproval`.\n\n## Generalize-forward\n\nExtract a shared helper only when the same logic is needed by both the API and the CLI, or by two tests; a single use stays inline. New public behaviour is added to `src/index.ts` first and then exposed by `src/cli.ts`.\n\n## Flag-first delivery\n\nA behaviour change that alters existing output ships behind an explicit opt-in option (CLI flag or API parameter) whose default keeps the current behaviour; the flag is removed in the roadmap phase that makes the new behaviour the default.\n\nhold: [] \u2014 release-only work (version bump, tag, promotion) is held until an explicit user ruling; publishing is out of scope for this private fixture.\n'''\nCONTENT['CLAUDE.md'] = r'''@AGENTS.md\nRun suite, typecheck and build gates through the host's memory-capped wrapper when the host requires one; the portable commands themselves are in README \u00a7Commands and roadmap/ro